GPUI Base and GPUI Component, licensed under Apache-2.0, for native controls.
Its bundled Lucide icons (https://lucide.dev/) use the ISC license, with
Feather-derived icons under MIT. Copyright 2026 Lucide Icons and Contributors;
copyright 2013-present Cole Bemis. See assets/LICENSE-LUCIDE.txt.

The app bundles unmodified IBM Plex Sans Regular and SemiBold and IBM Plex
Mono Regular (https://github.com/IBM/plex), licensed under OFL-1.1.
Copyright 2017-2018 IBM Corp. with Reserved Font Name "Plex".
The font license is in assets/OFL.txt. Font source revisions are in the
adjacent .license files.

The app bundles the unmodified Chatto icon from the web frontend, licensed
under Apache-2.0. Copyright 2026 ChattoCorp GmbH. See
assets/chatto-icon.png.license.

The app also uses these libraries:
- Axum (https://github.com/tokio-rs/axum) - MIT, for the loopback callback
- image (https://github.com/image-rs/image) - MIT OR Apache-2.0,
  for bounded raster decoding
- Chrono (https://github.com/chronotope/chrono) - MIT OR Apache-2.0,
  for local message times
- security-framework (https://github.com/kornelski/rust-security-framework) -
  MIT OR Apache-2.0, for macOS Keychain
- pulldown-cmark (https://github.com/pulldown-cmark/pulldown-cmark) - MIT,
  for Markdown parsing

The app includes the Chatto Rust SDK experiment, licensed under
EUPL-1.2.

The Rust client uses these libraries:
- sha2 (https://github.com/RustCrypto/hashes) - MIT OR Apache-2.0
- base64 (https://github.com/marshallpierce/rust-base64) - MIT OR Apache-2.0
- reqwest (https://github.com/seanmonstar/reqwest) - MIT OR Apache-2.0
- serde and serde_json (https://github.com/serde-rs) - MIT OR Apache-2.0
- url (https://github.com/servo/rust-url) - MIT OR Apache-2.0
- prost (https://github.com/tokio-rs/prost) - Apache-2.0
- futures-util (https://github.com/rust-lang/futures-rs) - MIT OR Apache-2.0
- uuid (https://github.com/uuid-rs/uuid) - MIT OR Apache-2.0
- Tokio (https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio) - MIT
- tokio-tungstenite (https://github.com/snapview/tokio-tungstenite) - MIT
- rustls (https://github.com/rustls/rustls) - Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT
  TLS uses rustls through reqwest and tokio-tungstenite.
